From 4055dc4d98fcd1c36a0b490273975632680288e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "T. Kurt Bond" <tkurtbond@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 13:13:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06/67] Round SHORT of a LONGREAL to REAL where it is used, not
 only where stored

OPV.Convert wrote no cast for a LONGREAL to REAL conversion, relying on
C's conversion on assignment. Inside an expression nothing converts, so
LONG(SHORT(x)) and SHORT(x) * 1.0D0 were x itself, not x rounded to
REAL. It now writes (REAL).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/compiler/OPV.Mod | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/compiler/OPV.Mod b/src/compiler/OPV.Mod
index 8e30da2b..4f811ae3 100644
--- a/src/compiler/OPV.Mod
+++ b/src/compiler/OPV.Mod
@@ -273,6 +273,10 @@
         OPM.Write(OpenParen); Entier(n, MinPrec); OPM.Write(CloseParen)
       ELSE OPM.WriteString("(CHAR)"); Entier(n, 9)
       END
+    ELSIF (to = OPT.Real) & (from = OPT.LReal) THEN
+      (* C converts implicitly only where the value is stored: LONG(SHORT(x))
+         and SHORT(x) used in a LONGREAL expression must round here. *)
+      OPM.WriteString("(REAL)"); expr(n, 9)
     ELSE expr(n, prec)
     END
   END Convert;
